From: ArmOS Project
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: use core GLSL for the macOS desktop blitter

macOS exposes OpenGL 3.2 and newer only through a core profile.  Its shader
compiler consequently rejects the GLSL 1.30 compatibility version hard-coded
in the internal VirGL blitter.  The renderer already selects its separate GLES
headers for an ES context, so select GLSL 1.50 core for desktop builds on Apple
and retain the upstream GLSL 1.30 contract everywhere else.

This covers every internal color, depth and multisample blitter shader through
the two shared desktop headers.  Guest shaders and advertised capsets remain
unchanged.

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_blitter.h b/src/vrend/vrend_blitter.h
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_blitter.h
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_blitter.h
@@ -29,8 +29,14 @@
 
 /* shaders for blitting */
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+#define VREND_DESKTOP_BLITTER_GLSL_HEADER "#version 150 core\n"
+#else
+#define VREND_DESKTOP_BLITTER_GLSL_HEADER "#version 130\n"
+#endif
+
 #define FS_HEADER_GL                               \
-   "#version 130\n"                             \
+   VREND_DESKTOP_BLITTER_GLSL_HEADER              \
    "// Blitter\n"                               \
    "%s"                                         \
 
@@ -48,7 +54,7 @@
 
 
 #define HEADER_GL                               \
-   "#version 130\n"                             \
+   VREND_DESKTOP_BLITTER_GLSL_HEADER              \
    "// Blitter\n"                               \
 
 #define HEADER_GLES                             \
